{{define "content" -}}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 id="boards-title">Leaderboards</h1>
  <p>Every board catlog is publishing. Flights flagged as cheated — teleports, refuels, resource edits, console use — score on none of them.</p>
</div>

{{- /* This list comes from the server, which builds it from the data: catlog
       keeps no list of celestial bodies, so a board for a place appears here
       once players have been there. Nothing in this template may assume how
       many rows there are. */}}
<div class="table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="All leaderboards">
<table id="boards-index">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Board</th>
      <th scope="col">Measured in</th>
      <th scope="col">Reads</th>
      <th scope="col" class="value">Players</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {{- range .Data.Boards}}
    <tr class="boards-row" data-stat="{{.Stat}}" data-ascending="{{.Ascending}}">
      <td><a href="{{statPath .Stat}}" class="board-link">{{.Title}}</a></td>
      {{- /* The display label, not the storage unit: this column has to agree
             with the header on the board page it links to. */}}
      <td class="muted unit">{{unitLabel .Unit}}</td>
      {{- /* Which way a board reads is published, never guessed: the career-time
             boards rank the smallest value first, and a reader that assumed
             otherwise would present the fastest ascent as the worst one. */}}
      <td class="direction muted">{{if .Ascending}}&#8595; lowest wins{{else}}&#8593; highest wins{{end}}</td>
      <td class="value" data-value="{{.Count}}">{{number .Count}}</td>
    </tr>
    {{- end}}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{{- if gt .Data.MinPlayers 1}}
<p id="boards-note" class="muted prose" style="margin-top: 1rem"><small>Boards for places, and for ways a vehicle came apart, come from what players actually did rather than from a list inside the server. One appears here once at least {{.Data.MinPlayers}} different players are on it. Before that it still exists, and still shows on the profile of whoever is on it — but a leaderboard with a single entrant is not a leaderboard.</small></p>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
